FerrionOS change to upstream RedoxFS (MIT license, kept), made against upstream commit 5ba45a6887374ab425326656a276bb3b62eba7dc after ferrion-passphrase-wipe.patch:
- redoxfs-key lists, adds (a passphrase, or a generated recovery key printed once), changes and removes key slots of a version 8 volume, on an image file or, as root, on the mounted root volume through a call on the mounted filesystem, and every change rewrites all headers of the ring.
- the daemon and the tools skip all-zero key slots, and the master keys a slot yields are checked against the header before use.
- redoxfs, redoxfs-mkfs, redoxfs-clone, redoxfs-resize and redoxfs-ar take --key-file PATH, or - for standard input, holding the exact passphrase bytes.
- creating a key refuses unless /scheme/rand/status reports seeded: yes.

